    "poster_id": 652,
    "post_rendered": "Circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/666f17d2caa22c20d29364a02823c4f95695ad4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W_1,W_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" > intersect at <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/c/59c44762c001c6348a67331ace6e4b76948d5889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P,K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" >.</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\"  width=\"30\" height=\"12\" > is common tangent of two circles which is nearer to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" > is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/a/08ae12b69f1364e6f0aa693d2a051b17383ea82a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > is on <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe6a61c0adf995408d4c70c51d35f9798bc472c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" >.</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/255140b38e3c950b5b5927eb6b6a72245cfaa7be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XP$\"  width=\"30\" height=\"12\" > intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe6a61c0adf995408d4c70c51d35f9798bc472c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" > for the second time in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e99ebdaa2b11d68e402f790ddc591b59c7ae4a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YP$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" > intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/a/08ae12b69f1364e6f0aa693d2a051b17383ea82a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" > in <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" >.</span> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"13\" > be intersection point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a4b9c32938e96f30b59dcb29f410cd4c2e3982.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX$\"  width=\"30\" height=\"12\" > and <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/5/4a56c1a130393e11539eb1f6ddcee8ebe4ce2c5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CY$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" >.</span> Prove that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" > is the second intersection point of circumcircles of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/0/bd04177a618735863023311466628751c3844633.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AXY$\"  width=\"44\" height=\"13\" ><br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/d/c4db3e48ee306cf574c3ac06758b919fb0ab887c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle QXA=\\angle QKP\\]\"  width=\"139\" height=\"16\" >",
    "post_canonical": "Circles $W_1,W_2$ intersect at $P,K$. $XY$ is common tangent of two circles which is nearer to $P$ and $X$ is on $W_1$ and $Y$ is on $W_2$. $XP$ intersects $W_2$ for the second time in $C$ and $YP$ intersects $W_1$ in $B$. Let $A$ be intersection point of $BX$ and $CY$. Prove that if $Q$ is the second intersection point of circumcircles of $ABC$ and $AXY$\n\\[\\angle QXA=\\angle QKP\\]",
